+### Resident bounded KV cache
+
+On 2026-10-05, frozen layers and stacks gain explicit `output,cache =
+model.prefill(prefix)` and `output,cache = model.decode(one_token,cache)`.
+Each layer keeps FP16 K/V with three GQA heads in fixed `(B,3,64,64)`
+device allocations. Prefill starts at position zero; decode accepts exactly
+one FP16 `(B,1,576)` token and a cache belonging to the same model. Total
+length is at most 64. The ordinary `forward` API still recomputes a full prefix.
+
+Device position selects RoPE, the updated cache slot and the causal mask;
+all positions reuse one static decode graph. K/V contents are immutable by
+contract, with new storage returned for each snapshot. Old snapshots may
+be reused or branched. Stacks preflight every cache and reject wrong owners,
+layer order, mixed prefill/decode branches, unequal lengths and full caches
+before executing any layer. Callers must not alter the state tensors.
+
+Compiler 8.3 rejects the original batch layout and late batch/head folding.
+The current one-token attention layout keeps internal N=1 before projection,
+RoPE and cache update, encoding samples in the head dimension with independent
+GQA indices and Softmax. B>1 decode now runs in one whole-batch attention
+submission, without sample selection or assembly. The same layout also fixes
+batched single-token prefill/forward compilation; longer prefill is unchanged.
+The compiler schedules internal tasks; this is not a measurement proving
+simultaneous sample or layer execution on hardware.
+The PyTorch native binding now supports independent multiple
+outputs, so attention output and K/V are bound directly to separate device
+allocations, removing the old packing and subsequent device-DMA splits.
+Position increment is a fourth attention output, eliminating its separate
+submission. Integer positions 1..64 are exact when incremented in FP16 and
+stored back as FP32; model arithmetic and genuine FP32 backend guarantees stay
+unchanged. After the previous DMA-assembly fusion, warm calls per layer were
+4/6/8/12 for B1/B2/B4/B8. Whole-batch attention reduces these to 4/4/4/4;
+prepared sample scalars are no longer needed. The prior B8=49 count
+included two first-decode gamma broadcasts; repeated warm calls confirm 47.
+There is no explicit host staging
+or per-position compilation. Initial compilation/preparation and segment
+boundary transfers are outside that claim; counters exclude driver DMA.
+
+The new offline demo combines a resident first-two/four-layer NPU segment
+with the remaining CPU layers' standard Transformers DynamicCache. CPU
+embedding/final norm/logits and explicit segment boundary transfers remain.
+This is an explicit inference pipeline, without general Transformers
+`generate()` integration, training, padding, W4A16 or longer contexts.
+Eight cached hybrid generations reproduce CPU tokens. In the initial single-output
+version's six warm timing groups, W8A16 decode was 1.26–1.97x slower than recomputing the full
+32/64-token prefix; B1/four layers takes 19.54 vs 15.52 ms, B4/four layers
+77.07 vs 40.67 ms. Functional caching does not establish a speed benefit.
+Those historical results remain in workspace `npunlock-probe/research/results/smollm-kv/REPORT.md`.
+New checks and same-process packed/multiple-output comparisons are in
+`npunlock-probe/research/results/smollm-kv-multi/REPORT.md`.
+In 21 interleaved same-process rounds, W8A16 decode latency falls 15.6–22.1%
+across six groups: four-layer B1 drops from 18.42 to 14.62 ms and B4 from
+74.89 to 59.91 ms. B1 is close to short-prefix recomputation; B4 remains
+slower, and all cached paths remain slower than the corresponding CPU FP16
+decode. Timings exclude initial compilation and segment transfers, include
+submissions/DMA/fences, and do not control desktop load or frequency.
+Rebuild the PyTorch extension with `build_torch_npu_device.ps1`; the session
+DLL and default RMSNorm kernel need no rebuild. `torch_npu_multi_output_demo.py`
+checks mixed dtype/shape outputs, allocation reuse, alias rejection, recovery
+after invalid bindings and legacy genuine FP32 arithmetic. Each output must
+cover a complete, independent allocation and may not alias any input/output.
+The position/sample fusion needs no native rebuild. Its 102 numerical records,
